# `$` prefix (documentation only)

In markdown and other prose, a `$` prefix marks an **ASC conceptual placeholder**. It is not a make target, not a pivot name, and not a shell variable (those stay `$HOME`, `$1`, etc. in scripts).

## Allowed

- `$subject` / `$action` (ASC "active" folder)
- `$subject` / `$object` / `$action` (ASC "active" folder)
- `$subject-$action` (entry point name or "pivot", used by make and in the DSL)
- `$subject--$predicate--$object` (describes relations)
- `$entity`
- `$field`

## Not allowed

Do not prefix ordinary names (pivots, tools, commands, files):

```text
❌ `$index` `$extract` `$relate` `$research` `$run-agent`
✅ index, extract, relate, research, run-agent
```
